1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 7th generation. 2283 BC to ? Son of Lu Zhong (陆终). Also known as Hui Lian (惠连).
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Madam Jin (金氏) who bore him a son - Xiong Qi (熊启).
2 CONT
2 CONT Commended for taming the river floods during the reign of Emperor Yao (尧帝). Was conferred the State of Can Hu (参胡) - in the present day Fenyang (芬阳) in Shanxi (山西) - by Emperor Yao. That was during the 96th year of his reign (2220
2 CONC  BC). Can Hu was renamed Huang State (黄国) and Hui Lian was given the surname Huang (黄) and name Yun (云) by the Emperor. According to legend, as the Emperor was about to confer a surname to Hui Lian, a huge band of yellow cloud app
2 CONC eared from the South. As a result, the Emperor chose the surname Huang (黄) and the name Yun (云).The descendants of Yun ruled the Huang State (黄国) until it was destroyed by Chu Cheng Wang (楚成王) of the Chu State (楚国) in 648 BC (僖十二年
2 CONC ), spanning 1,572 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT NB - There are several versions of the ranking of Yun (云). The generation rank of Yun adopted here is based on our Family Genealogy Book, Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu, (文明祖家谱) and Yanjingcun's Genealogy Book - Huang Shi Ying Zuo Fang Yuan Q
2 CONC u Wu Hao Zhi Pu (黄氏英佐房园趣无号支谱). It is consistent with that in the Huang Genealogy Book - Huang Shi Shi Sun Zu Pu (黄氏世孙族谱) and the Malaysian Huang Ancestral Genealogy Book - Ma Lai Xi Ya Huang Shi Zong Ci Zu Pu (马来西亚黄氏宗词族谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES (资料来源) -
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Huang Shi Ying Zuo Fang Yuan Qu Wu Hao Zhi Pu (黄氏英佐房园趣无号支谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. 黄氏世孙族谱.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. 马来西亚黄氏宗词族谱.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  Pre-Qin Period of China - YouTube (中国先秦时期疆域变化).
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.  楚成王 - 百度百科.
