1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Xiang Tu''' - From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Xiang Tu''' (Chinese: 相土; pinyin: Xiàng Tǔ; ? – ?) was an ancient Chinese noble, an ancestor of the Shang dynasty[1]. His family name is '''Zi''' (子), and his other name is '''Cheng Du''' (乘杜). His hometown is in Shangqiu (商丘),
2 CONC  Henan (河南),[2] and he was the third leader of the Shang nation.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''History'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Zhao Ming of Shang and thus the grandson of Xie of Shang,[3] being also an ancestor of the King Tang of Shang.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the beginning, people still did not know the horse-drawn cart is used for travel. It was said that he raised horses. The horse is tamed and trained, so the horse can pull the car and become one of the important means of transpo
2 CONC rtation.
2 CONT
2 CONT It can be seen that in the time of Xiang Tu, the Shang people have migrated from the nomadic life to the life of animal husbandry and agricultural cultivation. He developed forces in the east by force, on the coast of the Yellow S
2 CONC ea (黃海) and in the nearby islands.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT * Grandfather: Xie (契)
2 CONT ** – a son of the Emperor Ku of ancient China
2 CONT *** Father: Zhao Ming (昭明)
2 CONT ****Son: Chang Ruo (昌若)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xiang_Tu
