1 NAME Gōng Shū Zǔ, 公叔祖, 37
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gōng Shū Zǔ (公叔祖) was a historical figure from ancient China, estimated to have lived between 1492 BCE and 1372 BCE. He was the son of Zhū Áo (諸螯) and the father of Gǔ Gōng Dǎn Fù (古公亶父). His lineage is associated 
2 CONC with the Jī (姬) surname, which was the royal family name of the Zhou Dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interestingly, his descendants played a significant role in the establishment of the Zhou Dynasty, with his great-grandson, King Wu of Zhou, eventually overthrowing the Shang Dynasty. His family’s legacy is deeply intertwined with
2 CONC  the early history of Chinese civilization.
