1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xie,_Marquis_of_Jin
2 CONT
2 CONT Xie, Marquis of Jin
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search 
2 CONT
2 CONT Xie (燮)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marquis of Jin 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruler of Jin
2 CONT
2 CONT Predecessor Shu Yu of Tang 
2 CONT
2 CONT Successor Marquis Wu of Jin 
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Marquis Wu of Jin 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Shu Yu of Tang 
2 CONT
2 CONT Xie was the original Marquis of Jin (Chinese: 晉侯燮; pinyin: Jìn Hóu Xiè), and the second ruler of the State of Jin during the early Zhou Dynasty.[1] His ancestral name was Ji (姬), and given name Xie (燮) or Xiefu (燮父).
2 CONT
2 CONT Marquis Xie succeeded his father, Shu Yu of Tang, as the ruler of the state of Tang. During his reign, he moved the capital from Tang (唐) to Jinyang (晉陽) and renamed the state Jin.
2 CONT
2 CONT After he died, his son Ningzu succeeded him as Marquis Wu of Jin.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT References[edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Jump up ^ 가 나 정태현 : 《역주 춘추좌씨전》 6, 전통문화연구회, 2009년, ISBN 978-89-91729-26-8 94140, 80 ~ 81쪽 2.Jump up ^ Records of the Grand Historian
2 CONT
2 CONT Xie, Marquis of Jin
2 CONT
2 CONT House of Ji
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadet branch of the House of Ji
2 CONT
2 CONT Regnal titles
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by Shu Yu of Tang as Marquis of Tang Marquis of Jin Succeeded by Marquis Wu of Jin 
