1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cài Gòng Hóu (蔡共侯) was a ruler of the State of Cài (蔡国) during ancient China, estimated to have lived before 691 BCE. He was the son of Cài Lí Hóu (蔡釐侯) and the father of Cài Dài Hóu (蔡戴侯). His lineage was part of 
2 CONC the Jī (姬) surname, which was associated with the ruling family of the Zhou Dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT The State of Cài was a small but influential vassal state during the Zhou Dynasty, known for its contributions to Chinese culture and governance.
