1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Taken from http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Huan_of_Zhou
2 CONT
2 CONT King Huan of Zhou (Chinese: 周桓王; pinyin: Zhōu Húan Wáng; Wade–Giles: Chou Huan Wang; died 697 BC) was the fourteenth king of the Chinese Zhou Dynasty[3][4] and the second of the Eastern Zhou Dynasty (770-256 BC).
2 CONT
2 CONT His given name was Lín.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT King Huan’s father was King Ping’ son, Crown Prince Xiefu. Huan succeeded his grandfather in 719 BC.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son and successor of Huan was King Zhuang of Zhou.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 707 BC the royal forces were defeated in the military conflict with the Duke Zhuang of Zheng (r.743-701). The king himself was wounded.[7]
2 CONT
