1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The founding member of the Zeng (曾) family was Zeng Shen (曾參) who was one of the most filial and devote disciples of Confucius. Zeng Shen was born during the winter of the year of the fire monkey during the reign o
2 CONC f King Zhou Jing, on the 10th month, 12th day in current day Shandong Province in China. He lived from 505–436 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of 30, Shēn moved to Wucheng (also known as South Wucheng, which is now Jining City, Jiaxiang County, Shandong Province, China.  [参公三十岁移居武城（又称南武城，在今山东省济宁市嘉祥县满峒乡南武山村。一说费县，即今平邑魏庄乡).]
2 CONT
2 CONT Zeng Shen, who later became know as Zēngzǐ (曾子 Wade-Giles: Tsengtzu), courtesy name Ziyu (子輿), was a Chinese philosopher who authored of a large portion of the Great Learning (大學), including its foreword. His disciples are among t
2 CONC he most important compilers of the Analects of Confucius and other Confucian classics. Zengzi was also an early Chinese proponent of a round earth theory, as opposed to a flat earth model. In the Yuan dynasty, he was given the tit
2 CONC le Duke of Zhongshen (宗聖公) for "Elevating the Saint (Confucius)" and became one of the Four Sages of Confucianism along with Yan Hui (顏子), Zisi (子思), and Mencius (孟子). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zengzi http://www.chinaknowledge.de/History/Zhou/personszengzi.html
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Other Notes:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT King Zhou Jing (aka. Ji Gai) was the twenty-sixth sovereign of the Chinese Zhou Dynasty, the fourteenth of Eastern Zhou Dynasty, reigning from 520-476 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Confucius lived from 551-479 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Generation Numbers (70, 58, 5, 1世)''
2 CONT
2 CONT Zeng Shen is a 70th generation descendant of Chin Shi Huang Di (the Yellow Emperor), and following the same line:
2 CONT * a 59th generation descendant of Zēng Qū Liè 鄫曲烈, 13, 1世, 
2 CONT * 5th generation descendant of Zēng Wū 曾巫, 66, 54, 1世, and
2 CONT * the first generation (一世) of his branch of the Zeng Family
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Zeng Name Meaning''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.ancestry.com/name-origin?surname=Zeng Ancestry.com]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Chinese : from a simplified form of the name of the state of Kuai. During the Xia dynasty (2205–1766 bc) this state was granted to the youngest son of King Shaokang. After being overthrown by another state, the prince fled and ado
2 CONC pted a simplified form of the character Kuai as his surname.
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zeng Wikipedia]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Zeng (Chinese: 曾; pinyin: Zēng; Wade–Giles: Tseng) is a Chinese family name. In Cantonese, it is Tsang; in Taiwan, Tseng or Tzeng; in Malaysia, Chan; in Indonesia, Tjan; in Vietnam, Tăng. The surname Zeng is the 32nd most common s
2 CONC urname in Mainland China. It is the 16th most common surname in Taiwan.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.geni.com/people/S%C3%AC-Sh%C3%A0o-K%C4%81ng-%E5%A7%92%E5%B0%91%E5%BA%B7-12%E4%B8%96/6000000019932536584 Si Shao Kang] was the king of the Xia Dynasty, and he delegated one of his [http://www.geni.com/people/C%C3%A9ng-Q
2 CONC %C5%AB-Li%C3%A8-%E9%84%AB%E6%9B%B2%E7%83%88-13-1%E4%B8%96/6000000019932971265 sons] to rule the State of Zeng (Chinese: 鄫, 繒, 曾; pinyin: Zēng, Céng; Wade–Giles: Tseng, Ts'eng. Zeng was originally the name of a place) during the Sh
2 CONC ao Kang's reign. The Si's were the descendants of the King Yu of Xia (Si was the surname of the royal house of the Xia Dynasty). However in 567 BC, the State of Zeng was conquered by the State of Ju. Some of the royal members with
2 CONC  the surname Si including the [http://www.geni.com/people/Z%C4%93ng-W%C5%AB-%E6%9B%BE%E5%B7%AB-66-54-1%E4%B8%96/6000000019933189985 prince of Zeng] fled to the State of Lu. The Prince of Zeng gave his descendants the surname Zeng 
2 CONC in remembrance of the Zeng state.
