1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Taizu_of_Song '''Emperor Taizu of Song'''] (21 March 927 – 14 November 976), personal name '''Zhao Kuangyin''', courtesy name '''Yuanlang''', was the founder and first emperor
2 CONC  of the Song dynasty in China. He reigned from 960 until his death in 976. Formerly a distinguished military general of the Later Zhou dynasty, Emperor Taizu came to power after staging a coup d'état and forcing Emperor Gong, the 
2 CONC last Later Zhou ruler, to abdicate the throne in his favour.
2 CONT
2 CONT During his reign, Emperor Taizu conquered the states of Southern Tang, Later Shu, Southern Han and Jingnan, thus reunifying most of China proper and effectively ending the tumultuous Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms period. To stre
2 CONC ngthen his control, he lessened the power of military generals and relied on civilian officials in administration. He was succeeded by his younger brother, Zhao Kuangyi (Emperor Taizong).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Taizu_of_Song]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=9001 '''Zhao Kuangyin''' 趙匡胤] Zhao(1) Taizu [9001] Mingzi=Kuangyin. A Zhuozhou (Liao territory) resident, who was the second son of Hongyin [3198], a military officer. He was bor
2 CONC n in Luoyang. Taizong's [9002] elder brother, Xiaozong's [9011] 7th generation ancestor, Song(2) Wu's [7066] son-in-law, father-in-law of Wei(5) Xianxian [7093] and of Wang(2) Kechen's [1834] grandfather, Chengyan [3939], and Xian
2 CONC g(2) Zhuanfan's [7238] grandfather-in-law. His empress' younger sister was Zhang(1) Xun(1)'s [232] wife. Du(3) Chang [1721] was the grandson of his kin. His great great grandson Shien's [3209] father-in-law was Song(2) Shou (1575)
2 CONC 's brother. Shien's son-in-law, Song(2) Anguo [3788], was Song(2) Xiang's [8119] son. CBD, 4, 2935 (first empress, born He(4), who died in 958 at age 30 and was posthumously invested as empress after Taizu became emperor). CBD, 1,
2 CONC  761.From Hartwell's ACTIVITY table:954:  Apt. Dianqian Du yuhou (State Council)959:  Made Concurrently Du Dianjian (In State Council from 954 until he became emperor in 1/960). — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-col
2 CONC lection/46406 RMH] 
