1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=3543 '''Li Duanyi''' 李端懿] [3543] Ouyang Xiu, WJ, 32.6b-8b. Han Yuanji has son, and grandfather-in-law of Han(1) Qiu [632] (q.v.), as Yue, but no such son listed i
2 CONC n funerary inscription although all have radical 149 as generational indicator. The closest, assuming a copy error, would be son #1, Shen(2) [16824], which is the one I use. Duanyi was given a military title at age 7 and entered a
2 CONC s an attendant in the Eastern Palace of Zhenzong. Apparently the practice of granting a military title at the time a mingzi was given was extended to include close affinal kin of the imperial family and may have been a common prac
2 CONC tive among military officers in general. Duanyi was allowed to go to and from the palace as if he were a family member (jiaren). CBD, 2, 1048-9. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
